<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Justicia de Aragón</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12th century–<a href="/years/1707">1707</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Justiciar of Aragon, Justicia of Aragon, Justice of Aragon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Justicia de Aragón was the chief judge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-aragon">Kingdom of Aragon</a>, chosen from the knights, who settled disputes between the king and the nobility and guarded the kingdom's fueros. He could take people and property under his protection against royal officials, and in the 15th century the office became in practice irremovable. Philip II curbed it after the revolt of 1591, and it was abolished in 1707; it was revived in 1982 as an ombudsman.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/justicia-de-aragon.jpg" alt="Justicia de Aragón" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Msanmiguela · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Escudo_Color_Instituci%C3%B3n.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
